        "text": "The reference class base rate is the recent monthly annual inflation path for the same variant: not seasonally adjusted all-items CPI, Canada. The latest 12 fetched annual rates average 2.45 percent, while the latest four average 2.95 percent, so persistence around 3.0 percent is a better near-term prior than the full-year mean."
